# Windows-7-SP1 import allowlist (11-rust-implementation.md section 8).
# One "module!symbol" per line, case-insensitive; '#' starts a comment.
#
# This file proves "no import outside the reviewed set". It does NOT prove
# every entry is genuinely Windows-7-SP1-exported: no Windows 7 SP1 binary is
# available on this machine, so each provenance note below is an assertion
# recorded for review, not a measurement (design section 11, risk 4).
#
# ntoskrnl.exe!DbgPrint - present since Windows NT 3.1; long predates 7 SP1.
ntoskrnl.exe!DbgPrint
#
# Added by slice A3, from the built Win7 image's actual import table. Each
# provenance note below is an ASSERTION recorded for review, not a measurement:
# no Windows 7 SP1 binary is available on this machine (see the file header).
#
# ntoskrnl.exe!ExAllocatePoolWithTag - wdm.h declares it gated at NTDDI_WIN2K,
#   i.e. Windows 2000 and later; it is the documented pool allocator on the
#   Win7 baseline and is why this driver static-imports it rather than the
#   post-1507 ExAllocatePool2.
ntoskrnl.exe!ExAllocatePoolWithTag
# ntoskrnl.exe!ExFreePoolWithTag - the matching free, same NTDDI_WIN2K gate.
ntoskrnl.exe!ExFreePoolWithTag
# ntoskrnl.exe!MmGetSystemRoutineAddress - present since Windows 2000; it is
#   the mechanism 11-rust-implementation.md section 3 mandates for reaching a
#   post-baseline DDI, so it must itself be a baseline import.
ntoskrnl.exe!MmGetSystemRoutineAddress
# ksecdd.sys!BCryptGenRandom - kernel CNG. 11-rust-implementation.md section 4
#   states it "is available to the Win7 profile as well". That sentence is the
#   provenance; it has not been verified against a Windows 7 SP1 machine here,
#   and it is the entry in this file whose assertion carries the most weight.
ksecdd.sys!BCryptGenRandom

# Slice C3 direct imports measured from the built Win7X64 image. The C3 x64 and
# ARM64 package link maps attribute these import thunks to ntoskrnl.lib, not to
# the static Wdmsec archive; the Win7 image independently measures their
# presence. Header lines are from installed WDK 10.0.26100; each NTDDI gate
# predates Windows 7 SP1: exactly four rundown imports are gated at NTDDI_WINXP
# and the other eight are gated at NTDDI_WIN2K. These are documented/header-
# gate baseline assertions, not measurements against a Windows 7 kernel.
#
# ntoskrnl.exe!ExAcquireRundownProtection - direct ntoskrnl.lib;
